<title>CANADA: CN to sell Manitoba rail line.</title>
<headline>CN to sell Manitoba rail line.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian National Railway Co said on Friday it agreed to sell its 810-mile northern Manitoba rail network to  OmniTRAX, a Colorado-based shortline railroad operator.</p>
<p>Financial terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The sale, which includes a CN railyard, was expected to close next May, CNR said.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100</p>
